ProsperoSunshine: a failed read of a chunked body doesn't throw, and a server may refuse request bodies

Two of the places that report a failed read called on_error without looking whether one is set, as every other place does.
Sunshine sets none, so a chunked request whose connection ended inside a chunk threw std::bad_function_call out of the io
thread: one request from anybody who reaches the port, before any route or login, ended the server's start(). Both places
now look first.

Config::accept_content = false makes the server end a connection whose request announces a body (Content-Length above 0, or
chunked) before it reads any of it. Sunshine's GameStream servers set it (their patch 0032): no GameStream request has a
body, and waiting for one held a connection for timeout_content (300 s).

